The '''2026 Brentwood Borough Council election''' was held on 7 May 2026, alongside the [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]] being held on the same day, to elect 13 of 39 members of [[Brentwood Borough Council]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Election results from previous years {{!}} Brentwood Council |url=https://www.brentwood.gov.uk/election-results-from-previous-years |access-date=2026-01-29 |website=www.brentwood.gov.uk}}</ref>

== Background ==
In [[2024 Brentwood Borough Council election|2024]], the council remained under [[no overall control]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Brentwood result - Local Elections 2024 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2024/england/councils/E07000068 |access-date=2026-01-29 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> The [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] have run the council as a minority with [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] since [[2023 Brentwood Borough Council election|2023]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Dedman |first=Simon |date=2023-05-18 |title=Brentwood Council: Lib Dems to run authority with Labour |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-essex-65632290 |access-date=2026-01-29 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> In 2023, the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservatives]] lost their majority.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Meyler |first=Piers |date=2023-05-05 |title=Brentwood Council fails to keep full control as Tories lose three seats |url=https://www.essexlive.news/news/essex-news/brentwood-council-falls-keep-full-8412387 |access-date=2026-01-29 |website=Essex Live |language=en}}</ref>

